The temple you are referring to is the **Kunj Bihari Temple** (also known as *Kunj Bihari Mandir* or *Kunj Bihari Ji Temple*). 

Built in the 18th century near Sardar Market (the Clock Tower) and Gulab Sagar, it was commissioned by Gulab Rai, the influential concubine of Maharaja Vijay Singh of Marwar. As described by [Rama Toshi Arya's blog](w1), the shrine stands out for its architectural resemblance to the older Shri Ghanshyam Ji Temple and features an imposing marble toran entrance and a towering shikhara. High up inside the main *mandapa* hall, a wall mural depicts Gulab Rai together with Maharaja Vijay Singh in devotion to Lord Krishna.

