You should visit **Hierba Dulce**, a celebrated 100% plant-based restaurant in Oaxaca's historic center. 

Run entirely by women, the restaurant is dedicated to pre-Hispanic and traditional cooking styles, explicitly avoiding industrialized substitutes and processed ingredients. Instead, as noted by [Pure Wander](w2), they champion hyper-local, indigenous Mexican ingredients—such as heirloom native corn varieties, wild greens (*quelites*), local chilies, house-made moles, and fresh artisanal salsas—served in a peaceful open courtyard setting. It is widely praised by both vegan travelers and local guides for recreating authentic ancestral village flavors, according to [Your Friend the Nomad](w1).

{"map": [{"ref": "N6204371185"}]}

