A classic, cozy choice right in the heart of town is **Up for Breakfast**, an upstairs country diner located along Main Street in Manchester Center. 

Tucked into an intimate second-floor space, it has the quintessential Vermont morning diner feel and is well known for hearty plates like custom omelets, eggs with house hashes, and pancakes (often featuring flavors like pumpkin or seasonal fruits alongside real Vermont maple syrup), as noted by travelers on [Lyssy in the City](w1) and [Camera & Carry On](w2). It tends to get busy quickly in the mornings, so arriving early is recommended.

